"answer": "Project Zenith is a groundbreaking initiative aimed at optimizing cloud storage solutions for enhanced security and accessibility, with Marcus Cole as the project leader. The project kicked off in July 2023 (Q3) and has since expanded its team with experts in machine learning and cloud computing. The executive board approved a budget of $2 million, though a later update adjusted the budget to $550,000 due to unforeseen expenses, with an additional $55,000 allocated for compliance training and audits. Key milestones include initial findings in August showing a potential 20% efficiency increase via AI algorithms, and a breakthrough in predictive analytics in Phase Two. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought by the end of November, with detailed reports and discussions scheduled for meetings in August, November, and beyond."
